Package: hotcoldESF
Type: Package
Title: Covariate-Adjusted Hot and Cold Spots by Eigenvector Spatial Filtering
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yandira", "Cuvero", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yandira.cuvero@gmail.com"),
    person("Rowan", "Cherodian", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8951-7932")),
    person("Jorge", "Mateu", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2868-7604")),
    person("Carlos", "Almeida", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7301-963X")))
Description: Maps hot and cold spots of area-level counts after adjusting for
    covariates. A hot (cold) spot is an area whose spatially structured
    residual is positive (negative) and larger than spatially unstructured
    noise would produce. The residuals of a regression on the covariates are
    first tested for spatial autocorrelation with Moran's I and its exact
    moments (Tiefelsdorf and Griffith, 2007) <doi:10.1068/a37378>. The spatial
    component is then estimated by eigenvector spatial filtering with a ridge
    penalty chosen by cross-validation, each area is labelled hot, cold or
    neutral with a permutation band, and the areas are ordered into a priority
    list. Getis-Ord Gi* and local Moran's I are included as benchmarks.
